WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.489
- Melted cheese on top of
bread, is that a sandwich?

00:00:02.489 --> 00:00:03.322
- [Ned] That is a sandwich.

00:00:03.322 --> 00:00:05.129
- So a pizza's a sandwich, Ned?

00:00:05.129 --> 00:00:07.629
- Unfortunately, yes.
- No, no!

00:00:12.409 --> 00:00:13.831
- You might love hotdogs.

00:00:13.831 --> 00:00:15.286
You might love sandwiches.

00:00:15.286 --> 00:00:17.889
But is that hotdog also a sandwich?

00:00:17.889 --> 00:00:18.908
Today we're gonna get to the bottom

00:00:18.908 --> 00:00:20.575
of this once and for all. Let's go.

00:00:20.575 --> 00:00:21.867
- I think hotdogs are sandwiches.

00:00:21.867 --> 00:00:23.839
- And I think hotdogs are not sandwiches.

00:00:23.839 --> 00:00:27.349
- I believe that hotdogs are sandwiches.

00:00:27.349 --> 00:00:28.711
- I'm holding one sandwich,

00:00:28.711 --> 00:00:30.549
but that is also a sandwich and a hotdog.

00:00:30.549 --> 00:00:33.466
- A hotdog is a hotdog, my friends.

00:00:35.748 --> 00:00:38.378
- The logic is that the
definition of a sandwich is

00:00:38.378 --> 00:00:40.660
some sort of filling in between bread.

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:42.370
- Technically, it's not in between.

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:44.554
It's laying on the bread.

00:00:44.554 --> 00:00:48.028
- I know colloquially we all
know hotdogs aren't sandwiches,

00:00:48.028 --> 00:00:50.821
but we're a society built on rules.

00:00:50.821 --> 00:00:53.385
As it stands, you have to look at

00:00:53.385 --> 00:00:54.628
how the dictionary's written.

00:00:54.628 --> 00:00:56.371
- It's like rectangles and squares.

00:00:56.371 --> 00:00:58.361
A square is a rectangle, but
a rectangle's not a square.

00:00:58.361 --> 00:01:01.227
Just because you don't
call a hotdog a sandwich

00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:02.323
doesn't mean it's not a sandwich.

00:01:02.323 --> 00:01:04.327
It's still technically a sandwich.

00:01:04.327 --> 00:01:05.805
You just call it a hotdog.

00:01:05.805 --> 00:01:07.715
- I gotta interject here 'cause
this is driving me crazy.

00:01:07.715 --> 00:01:09.208
I think that your logic is flawed.

00:01:09.208 --> 00:01:10.913
I think people and the
way language is used--

00:01:10.913 --> 00:01:12.443
- Zack, why bother even
having a dictionary?

00:01:12.443 --> 00:01:14.038
- Ned, can I get my argument out?

00:01:14.038 --> 00:01:16.341
- Nobody is trying to argue
that a hotdog is not a hotdog.

00:01:16.341 --> 00:01:17.678
That would be ridiculous.

00:01:17.678 --> 00:01:19.694
I'm just arguing that
it is also a sandwich.

00:01:19.694 --> 00:01:23.194
- You have commitment problems, my friend.

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:27.847
- If you say that a hotdog is a sandwich,

00:01:27.847 --> 00:01:29.247
all of a sudden, anything
can be a sandwich.

00:01:29.247 --> 00:01:30.907
We believe that an open-faced sandwich

00:01:30.907 --> 00:01:32.196
is a sandwich, correct?

00:01:32.196 --> 00:01:33.705
- Avocado toast, yes.

00:01:33.705 --> 00:01:36.089
- Okay, so what about melted
cheese on top of bread?

00:01:36.089 --> 00:01:37.369
Is that a sandwich?
- That is a sandwich.

00:01:37.369 --> 00:01:39.225
- So a pizza's a sandwich, Ned?

00:01:39.225 --> 00:01:41.127
- Unfortunately, yes.
- No, no!

00:01:41.127 --> 00:01:42.923
- If you want a hotdog,

00:01:42.923 --> 00:01:44.324
how will you tell that to your friends?

00:01:44.324 --> 00:01:45.730
- I would say I want a hotdog.

00:01:45.730 --> 00:01:48.234
- So a hotdog is a hotdog,
not a motherfuckin' sandwich.

00:01:48.234 --> 00:01:50.833
You wouldn't say "Go
get a sandwich," right?

00:01:50.833 --> 00:01:51.855
'Cause then what would happen?

00:01:51.855 --> 00:01:55.048
- Because a hotdog is not the
most readily available image

00:01:55.048 --> 00:01:57.476
of a sandwich does not
make it not a sandwich.

00:01:57.476 --> 00:01:58.761
- Eugene, get in here.

00:01:58.761 --> 00:02:00.775
Is pizza a sandwich?

00:02:00.775 --> 00:02:01.859
- No, it is not.

00:02:01.859 --> 00:02:04.537
- Is a hotdog a sandwich?

00:02:04.537 --> 00:02:05.370
- Fuck, no!

00:02:05.370 --> 00:02:06.494
- Damn right, Ned!

00:02:06.494 --> 00:02:09.326
- You don't see sandwiches
sold in hotdog places.

00:02:09.326 --> 00:02:13.159
You don't see hotdogs
sold in sandwich places.

00:02:18.169 --> 00:02:20.126
- You know, it's all
about perception, okay?

00:02:20.126 --> 00:02:21.748
I honestly don't even really
like hotdogs that much,

00:02:21.748 --> 00:02:23.129
but I just don't think they're sandwiches.

00:02:23.129 --> 00:02:26.581
- If you think it's about
perception verses facts,

00:02:26.581 --> 00:02:28.981
then saying a hotdog is not a sandwich

00:02:28.981 --> 00:02:31.314
is just an alternative fact.

00:02:32.547 --> 00:02:34.714
(sobbing)

00:02:39.474 --> 00:02:41.894
- I believe that you
have to stand for things,

00:02:41.894 --> 00:02:45.345
and once you start making
words encompass everything,

00:02:45.345 --> 00:02:46.717
society falls to shit.

00:02:46.717 --> 00:02:48.314
- I get the other side. I get it.

00:02:48.314 --> 00:02:50.722
But something about
calling a hotdog a sandwich

00:02:50.722 --> 00:02:52.598
just makes my blood curl.

00:02:52.598 --> 00:02:54.057
I don't know what it is.

00:02:54.057 --> 00:02:56.015
I can't describe it scientifically,

00:02:56.015 --> 00:02:57.971
like in a dictionary like Jordan can,

00:02:57.971 --> 00:02:59.071
but sometimes,

00:02:59.071 --> 00:03:00.660
you just have a really
strong feeling about things,

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:01.954
and you just know you're
right, and I'm right.

00:03:01.954 --> 00:03:03.149
Whatever, bye.

00:03:03.149 --> 00:03:05.298
- If Merriam-Webster
changes the dictionary,

00:03:05.298 --> 00:03:06.381
I'll change my side.

00:03:06.381 --> 00:03:07.622
- People who think that
hotdogs are sandwiches,

00:03:07.622 --> 00:03:09.098
this is the person whose team you're on.

00:03:09.098 --> 00:03:10.859
The person who's saying
that pizza's a sandwich.

00:03:10.859 --> 00:03:13.531
If you believe that pizza's
a sandwich, I can't help you.

00:03:13.531 --> 00:03:14.963
- It is interesting that you said

00:03:14.963 --> 00:03:16.528
you know, "something in between breads".

00:03:16.528 --> 00:03:18.152
Kind of made me think a little bit.

00:03:18.152 --> 00:03:19.228
Like what is a sandwich?

00:03:19.228 --> 00:03:20.604
What makes things things?

00:03:20.604 --> 00:03:22.699
What is life, you know?

00:03:22.699 --> 00:03:24.532
So, thank you, Jordan.

00:03:25.928 --> 00:03:27.011
- Please hug.

00:03:30.712 --> 00:03:32.041
(laughs)

